function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $y - 2\\ne0$.\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=-2$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= \\frac{c^{2} - 4}{c - 2} \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=-3$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= \\frac{c^{2} - 4}{c - 2} \\\\  &= -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=2$, $y - 2=\\left(2\\right) - 2=0$ violates the original domain. This is *not* an equilibrium solution; cancellation cannot restore an excluded value.\n\nSelect $y=-2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c668f4f-a0bc-5d99-9904-0e04f7c786a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694219} {:answer/id #uuid "69df3d45-2d06-5276-b096-ea53e3c78b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c668f4f-a0bc-5d99-9904-0e04f7c786a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694219} :answer-field/id #uuid "08a4a048-b36e-5437-900c-8cdbfcdd41aa" :answer-field/key "$y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694217} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "031cab38-2801-542b-8eb5-504f306cb38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694215} {:answer/id #uuid "fdabbf39-b2fe-5a8e-8eda-bfdab16aaccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "031cab38-2801-542b-8eb5-504f306cb38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694215} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d58b871-bfa6-55a0-8281-34ffdac1af1b" :answer-field/key "$y=- \\frac{1}{e}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22668b5f-9ff0-539f-ab9b-26a09fb42b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694220} {:answer/id #uuid "c90a615b-2d94-528b-b0ef-5f5e14e00b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c90a615b-2d94-528b-b0ef-5f5e14e00b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694247} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5db91c9-2c46-52bd-9060-b657c52def1b" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694251}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34f63703-f444-5ba9-9a19-b083a44dab6e" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\left(- y - e^{-1}\\right) \\ln{\\left(- y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $- y>0$.\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=- \\frac{1}{e}$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(- c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)} \\\\  &= -1 \\\\ L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(- c - e^{-1}\\right) \\ln{\\left(- c \\right)} \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=-1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(- c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(- c - e^{-1}\\right) \\ln{\\left(- c \\right)} \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=0$, $- y=- \\left(0\\right)=0$ violates the original domain. This is *not* an equilibrium solution; cancellation cannot restore an excluded value.\n\nSelect $y=- \\frac{1}{e}$ and $y=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3196510e-dfea-54da-8291-9f747aef2d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694226} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b30b83-735a-593d-aae7-450c7c6c6f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3196510e-dfea-54da-8291-9f747aef2d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694226} :answer-field/id #uuid "67ad5b9e-b652-5fcf-8bcd-5fbca0f01083" :answer-field/key "$y=e^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27dab719-96d4-50a4-9bbb-3b96099648e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694222} {:answer/id #uuid "2dff4fb3-4eea-574c-a7ee-f29b8b1a5726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27dab719-96d4-50a4-9bbb-3b96099648e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694222} :answer-field/id #uuid "697a254f-5adf-5920-b388-f1a6e7f837c4" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4239754-9c54-5105-8149-fa639d7ee4a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694250} {:answer/id #uuid "f6751190-6867-53b8-acd7-7c985be935ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4239754-9c54-5105-8149-fa639d7ee4a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694250} :answer-field/id #uuid "739abb3c-9f6f-5193-9de2-24257a3be607" :answer-field/key "$y=e^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694238}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a17a012d-e1ff-5129-9f9b-a3bfe77267a8" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\left(y - e^{2}\\right) \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $y>0$.\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=e^{2}$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{2} \\right)} \\\\  &= 2 \\\\ L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(c - e^{2}\\right) \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=e^{-1}$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)} \\\\  &= -1 \\\\ L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(c - e^{2}\\right) \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} \\\\  &= - \\frac{1}{e} + e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=-1$, $y=\\left(-1\\right)=-1$ violates the original domain. This is *not* an equilibrium solution; cancellation cannot restore an excluded value.\n\nSelect $y=e^{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c731832-8ca4-50f2-b91e-cd5ecbcb8899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694267} {:answer/id #uuid "46479283-edcd-5402-88e1-c2437b6695d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c731832-8ca4-50f2-b91e-cd5ecbcb8899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694267} :answer-field/id #uuid "3824feb8-5194-597e-afff-177a721dca33" :answer-field/key "$y=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "598c218b-359f-5c6c-b395-ecffa84b7c76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694270} {:answer/id #uuid "8fcb6e53-f182-5215-8955-eda7472a3a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fcb6e53-f182-5215-8955-eda7472a3a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694279} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa70cb47-95c9-599f-9cae-78ca6cfec83a" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694285} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd2f0f87-0dad-5195-be62-6727bc74b942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694288} {:answer/id #uuid "d455974b-6375-5843-b69e-303001a717d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d455974b-6375-5843-b69e-303001a717d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694289} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2225cd3-d7e6-58e6-bda1-15183da75112" :answer-field/key "$y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694286}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "053da273-e1a4-5e66-ae67-f15ce48890c4" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} + \\left(y\\right) = y + \\frac{- y^{2} - 4 y}{\\left(y + 2\\right)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $y + 2\\ne0$.\n\nIsolating the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = - \\frac{y \\left(y + 4\\right)}{y^{2} + 4 y + 4}.\n$$\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= c \\\\  &= 1 \\\\ R(c) &= c + \\frac{- c^{2} - 4 c}{\\left(c + 2\\right)^{2}} \\\\  &= \\frac{4}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=-3$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= c \\\\  &= -3 \\\\ R(c) &= c + \\frac{- c^{2} - 4 c}{\\left(c + 2\\right)^{2}} \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=0$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= c \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= c + \\frac{- c^{2} - 4 c}{\\left(c + 2\\right)^{2}} \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80dc5312-3b19-50f7-8fb0-2e59f35a08b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694277} {:answer/id #uuid "98ccfadc-0034-506c-9528-2f2ca31fe64a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98ccfadc-0034-506c-9528-2f2ca31fe64a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694281} :answer-field/id #uuid "02c29649-2059-5594-8755-eb15f1f044d6" :answer-field/key "$y=e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ac36d87-5a89-56b8-9c1a-229a31370647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694274} {:answer/id #uuid "f28e7014-b34f-50a7-8675-a039741d69b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ac36d87-5a89-56b8-9c1a-229a31370647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694274} :answer-field/id #uuid "671db1ac-9c71-555b-a538-a6e797a9435f" :answer-field/key "$y=e^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694273} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180ff976-68fa-5b17-9df5-0594d53e4df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694261} {:answer/id #uuid "21261a1e-24e4-52ab-aeec-d5243a2239fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21261a1e-24e4-52ab-aeec-d5243a2239fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694263} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5c56132-4b09-5a08-ae07-ec3f55103c97" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694291}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0b2fbcb7-3dca-5ad2-aaef-9978fc6abbe5" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} + \\left(y\\right) = y^{2} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} + y.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $y>0$.\n\nIsolating the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = y^{2} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=e$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\  &= 1 \\\\ L(c) &= c \\\\  &= e \\\\ R(c) &= c^{2} \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} + c \\\\  &= e + e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ L(c) &= c \\\\  &= 1 \\\\ R(c) &= c^{2} \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} + c \\\\  &= 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=e^{-1}$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)} \\\\  &= -1 \\\\ L(c) &= c \\\\  &= e^{-1} \\\\ R(c) &= c^{2} \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} + c \\\\  &= - \\frac{1}{e^{2}} + e^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "608e11cc-28a2-550b-82a2-e1a316612184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694271} {:answer/id #uuid "7a5ff375-46ab-571a-9e77-ffdd28f7c46b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a5ff375-46ab-571a-9e77-ffdd28f7c46b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694275} :answer-field/id #uuid "2030e042-eb8b-5cd4-8d7e-d42a058e164c" :answer-field/key "$y=- e + 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e300cda-ca44-5de4-883f-53efe7fb5055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694269} {:answer/id #uuid "809dfa40-5a2d-56bc-96a2-4bfc5afd71f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e300cda-ca44-5de4-883f-53efe7fb5055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694269} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f05ab2d-f7cc-5dbd-91cd-16cc619eb07b" :answer-field/key "$y=- \\frac{1}{e} + 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694265} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e868595-3f36-57b7-adc0-2969c9cf5cd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694283} {:answer/id #uuid "f6cf5a99-db60-5074-98bc-fba0c03e4390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6cf5a99-db60-5074-98bc-fba0c03e4390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694292} :answer-field/id #uuid "62341a38-c1e1-5967-9a1f-3962891642af" :answer-field/key "$y=- e^{2} + 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694272}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8de248b-bc37-5098-a790-386c57451f53" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} + \\left(2 y - 1\\right) = \\left(2 y - 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(- y + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(- y + 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $- y + 1>0$.\n\nIsolating the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = y^{2} \\ln{\\left(- y + 1 \\right)} - 2 y \\ln{\\left(- y + 1 \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(- y + 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}.\n$$\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=- e^{2} + 1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(- c + 1 \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{2} \\right)} \\\\  &= 2 \\\\ L(c) &= 2 c - 1 \\\\  &= - 2 e^{2} + 1 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(2 c - 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(- c + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(- c + 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right) \\\\  &= - 2 e^{2} + e^{-2} + 1 + 2 e^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=- \\frac{1}{e} + 1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(- c + 1 \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)} \\\\  &= -1 \\\\ L(c) &= 2 c - 1 \\\\  &= - \\frac{2}{e} + 1 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(2 c - 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(- c + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(- c + 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right) \\\\  &= - \\frac{2}{e} + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=- e + 1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(- c + 1 \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\  &= 1 \\\\ L(c) &= 2 c - 1 \\\\  &= - 2 e + 1 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(2 c - 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(- c + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(- c + 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right) \\\\  &= - 2 e + e^{-2} + 1 + e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=- \\frac{1}{e} + 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9564586b-4057-504a-be80-c2168e72b0bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694280} {:answer/id #uuid "9db72884-07c5-5fb4-8bd4-d19353e244cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9db72884-07c5-5fb4-8bd4-d19353e244cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694282} :answer-field/id #uuid "075fc967-b6bd-58a2-b56e-91c09d11f769" :answer-field/key "$y=1 + e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "877e11ad-2692-5866-b42c-763f0b7313dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694278} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a4a5f5-b9fa-5969-ad89-82ea0adc444c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5a4a5f5-b9fa-5969-ad89-82ea0adc444c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694287} :answer-field/id #uuid "1160abe9-3571-510c-8943-7b15e7aae871" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14289bd2-4cb1-5a13-bb6e-85ccb2f0b7d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694260} {:answer/id #uuid "2d12595b-6a50-5a08-8952-c3a49e86fdcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14289bd2-4cb1-5a13-bb6e-85ccb2f0b7d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694260} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe02ca87-43fa-5387-b5a0-b648e2dd45bf" :answer-field/key "$y=e^{-1} + 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694293}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe198673-508e-5cdd-80a3-449f65da96c3" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dy}{dt}= \\\\ \\left(y - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} \\\\ + e^{-2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y - 1>0$.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(c)= \\\\ \\left(c - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} \\\\ + e^{-2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\n- For $c=1 + e$: Use $\\ln{\\left(e \\right)}=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(1 + e)= \\\\ e^{-2} + e^{2} \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\ =e^{-2} + e^{2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=2$: Use $\\ln{\\left(1 \\right)}=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=1 \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} + e^{-2} \\\\ &=e^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=e^{-1} + 1$: Use $\\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)}=-1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(e^{-1} + 1)= \\\\ \\frac{\\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)}}{e^{2}} + e^{-2} \\\\ =0\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=e^{-1} + 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748212 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a15c633-1ac4-540c-9d98-1121a23b73a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748207} {:answer/id #uuid "c951d591-36af-57de-955b-0943250e8f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c951d591-36af-57de-955b-0943250e8f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748329} :answer-field/id #uuid "71bb6d1c-8a90-5844-98d7-dc1c089860e5" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "423420d6-e204-5aa2-b4d6-1139c461d60d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748238} {:answer/id #uuid "9caac882-3e42-5e84-b456-e36f110f62ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "423420d6-e204-5aa2-b4d6-1139c461d60d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748238} :answer-field/id #uuid "972df4ac-2d1a-5501-9978-f4e8e7734d91" :answer-field/key "$y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aac168c-3e5e-581a-82e4-1766bee73f22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748284} {:answer/id #uuid "b278c1db-59e5-5661-ac87-59d15d62c09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aac168c-3e5e-581a-82e4-1766bee73f22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748284} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0da39d0-8dfa-57ae-be8e-a04422abdd64" :answer-field/key "$y=-1 + e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748315}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "141a55c9-d09e-52ce-941e-f884a7716745" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dy}{dt}= \\\\ \\left(y + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(y + 1 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y + 1>0$.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(c)= \\\\ \\left(c + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(c + 1 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\n- For $c=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=4 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-1 + e$: Use $\\ln{\\left(e \\right)}=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1 + e) &=e^{2} \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\ &=e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$: Use $\\ln{\\left(1 \\right)}=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) &=1 \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84e2426d-9388-5767-918f-6aaede1a885c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748278} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb8c48b-b026-5fd1-a705-3d7d96626cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbb8c48b-b026-5fd