{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "368851c4-156d-54b1-afce-4750f12eec6e" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = - y^{2} - 3 y - 2\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = - c^{2} - 3 c - 2\n$$\n\n- For $c=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=-3 - 2 - 1 \\\\ &=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) &=-2 - 1 + 3 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) &=-4 - 2 + 6 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-1$ and $y=-2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da784627-cbb1-59c2-8a08-10520a8e0945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748347} {:answer/id #uuid "e42ec4b7-88fe-5a92-a1d0-866d48c557fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e42ec4b7-88fe-5a92-a1d0-866d48c557fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748354} :answer-field/id #uuid "45774ddf-32b6-5d7c-86d7-77e6f32e6dd5" :answer-field/key "$y=-4$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7795627-ed92-5c86-b3c4-20faf468c3e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748321} {:answer/id #uuid "ecee0e4f-ba63-5ccd-8558-d5943cb20d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748358}] :answer-fiel