hered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $- y - 1>0$.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(c)= \\\\ \\left(- c - e - 1\\right) \\ln{\\left(- c - 1 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\n- For $c=-3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(-3)= \\\\ \\left(- e + 2\\right) \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(-4)= \\\\ \\left(- e + 3\\right) \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-2$: Use $\\ln{\\left(1 \\right)}=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(-2)= \\\\ \\left(- e + 1\\right) \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} \\\\ =0\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$, $- c - 1=-1$ violates the original domain, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b8340a6-1ed7-5ffa-95bf-17b6d756d142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748286} {:answer/id #uuid "ee839620-8ecf-5cf2-abcd-d111178348aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b8340a6-1ed7-5ffa-95bf-17b6d756d142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748286} :answer-field/id #uuid "6213c2ab-4c93-579a-b779-d8a55ed55de9" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bda8fd1d-7b73-53de-a921-bf7ba5021988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748322} {:answer/id #uuid "d74cee56-8479-5360-b59d-db58752d3150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bda8fd1d-7b73-53de-a921-bf7ba5021988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748322} :answer-field/id #uuid "b47e5247-b584-597e-8399-dfdaf2dbfd34" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8501d68c-9526-5346-abbc-e0cc09aab67a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748279} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ec6879-9aa5-51eb-878f-cdf0c02b9c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8501d68c-9526-5346-abbc-e0cc09aab67a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748279} :answer-field/id #uuid "cac1764f-530e-52f9-93e4-fc05d44ce5a2" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748333}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c85940e-5d6a-5e77-8c03-607d21fd581c" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dy}{dt}= \\\\ \\frac{y^{2} - 1}{y^{2}}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y\\ne0$.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = \\frac{c^{2} - 1}{c^{2}}\n$$\n\n- For $c=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=1$ and $y=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6708f499-476c-55b4-8ca0-00f4c3349687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748262} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8b94d3-e886-5c36-905c-593be9af371b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6708f499-476c-55b4-8ca0-00f4c3349687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748262} :answer-field/id #uuid "669e614d-b7e5-59d8-9a23-d2d2fba2e766" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54e27c5c-6fbd-5b53-977e-7a3f137734c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748252} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fbf5f0-6601-567e-b4a4-a12aa8dcb7cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8fbf5f0-6601-567e-b4a4-a12aa8dcb7cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748328} :answer-field/id #uuid "72418077-679e-5a1d-bd03-b0093496599c" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a488546a-8e6d-53a5-b90f-557bead28c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748307} {:answer/id #uuid "eb0a5ab9-f798-573c-98cd-eb44e827d1c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a488546a-8e6d-53a5-b90f-557bead28c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748307} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb0e56df-fa8d-5a25-bce8-c3e5fb3515f0" :answer-field/key "$y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748334}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4db980ed-67fb-5185-9224-78c8f7859f26" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} -2 = y^{3} - y^{2}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nRearranging once, test whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = c^{3} - c^{2} + 2\n$$\n\n- For $c=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=-4 + 2 + 8 \\\\ &=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) &=-1 - 1 + 2 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) &=0 + 0 + 2 \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748280 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35d495ab-3e1c-585c-8caf-fd387e9baf19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748233} {:answer/id #uuid "dff5fcbd-d7a9-5d45-a9fd-a0dd0eb8c3f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35d495ab-3e1c-585c-8caf-fd387e9baf19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748233} :answer-field/id #uuid "cca55b19-2945-5c4e-86b5-a4d3e0c66208" :answer-field/key "$y=- \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748336} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8b02b61-d28d-5e14-90f5-a81a0e65b583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748327} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5ef06f-1ba9-507a-b957-67c58106344f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca5ef06f-1ba9-507a-b957-67c58106344f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f237acb7-6045-560e-8466-8203a3e4c3df" :answer-field/key "$y=1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b98761c-9c7f-558c-9c43-d528d467da4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748226} {:answer/id #uuid "84deefac-6bc4-5706-9ccf-c57bb40b9668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84deefac-6bc4-5706-9ccf-c57bb40b9668" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748277} :answer-field/id #uuid "fed39b0d-a6e9-5537-920a-d6dbe1ac1915" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86972ed0-fdb5-5c6a-a3da-dc7cbd5ab885" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dy}{dt}= \\\\ 2 \\sin{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = 2 \\sin{\\left(c - 1 \\right)}\n$$\n\n- For $c=- \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 1$: Use $\\sin{\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=-1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(- \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 1)= \\\\ 2 \\sin{\\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\\\ =-2\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1$: Use $\\sin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=2 \\sin{\\left(0 \\right)} \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$: Use $\\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(1 + \\frac{\\pi}{2})= \\\\ 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\\\ =2\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08de2780-3edc-5ba6-874b-a413d566d130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748206} {:answer/id #uuid "842fe03d-2bf0-5408-ac9b-30da9c391361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "842fe03d-2bf0-5408-ac9b-30da9c391361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748275} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf7172d-3765-5c7e-924d-bb0ea9356bb5" :answer-field/key "$y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44927a65-3ee0-52c6-9f97-2529b386810c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748240} {:answer/id #uuid "9b4a8b16-0f24-5908-873b-3d636136f742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b4a8b16-0f24-5908-873b-3d636136f742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748300} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac6e1afa-f3ac-532a-9e4d-e54edb64d9d0" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "317fcba7-b54f-51b1-bd98-e507f4b8e322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748231} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc095cd-9812-57ce-9f2d-d05133950a22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "317fcba7-b54f-51b1-bd98-e507f4b8e322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748231} :answer-field/id #uuid "f250119f-3e90-51e7-b516-d3abb3cac046" :answer-field/key "$y=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748363}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b528cf2-db44-5164-a8ce-4d256d541071" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} + 4 y = - 2 y^{2}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nRearranging once, test whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = - 2 c^{2} - 4 c\n$$\n\n- For $c=-2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) &=-8 + 8 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=-4 - 2 \\\\ &=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) &=0 + 0 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-2$ and $y=0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a121ea3c-2e7a-5f30-85dd-ec9a0e046fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748304} {:answer/id #uuid "da815514